
Local RAG Product & Support Assistant

A lightweight, self-hosted Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) backend powered by Ollama, ChromaDB, and FastAPI. It exposes a unified /api/chat endpoint so external web, mobile, or desktop applications can embed an autonomous assistant that answers product and operational questions directly.

1. System Overview & Objectives

• Core Purpose: Answer customer questions using local markdown documentation (product specs, pricing, and support procedures like password resets) without hallucinating.
• External Consumption: Acts as a headless microservice consumed via standard HTTP POST requests by any client application.
• Zero-Policy Friction: Users get direct, grounded answers inside the host application without needing to read external help centers or guidelines.
• Air-Gapped Privacy: Runs completely locally via Ollama (llama3.2:3b and nomic-embed-text), keeping data off third-party servers.

