6. External Application Integration Contract

External host applications integrate by sending an HTTP POST request to http://<host-ip>:8000/api/chat.

Request Payload (application/json)

json
{
  "message": "How do I reset my password?",
  "session_id": "user-app-session-9821"
}
Use code with caution.

Response Payload (application/json)

json
{
  "reply": "Go to the login page, click 'Forgot Password', and enter your email. The reset link is valid for 30 minutes.",
  "sources": ["docs/support/password_reset.md"]
}
Use code with caution.

Example Client Integration (JavaScript / Fetch)

javascript
async function askAppAssistant(userQuestion, sessionId = "web-client-1") {
  const response = await fetch("http://localhost:8000/api/chat", {
    method: "POST",
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    body: JSON.stringify({ message: userQuestion, session_id: sessionId })
  });

  if (!response.ok) {
    throw new Error(`Assistant error: ${response.statusText}`);
  }

  const data = await response.json();
  return data.reply; // Render directly in your app's chat widget
}
